      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T11:34:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per discussion, the code in this method doesn\u0027t actually implement this behaviour. If this network were the best network for a request, it wouldn\u0027t reach here (and if it did, it might get torn at line 5316 because if it was validated it wouldn\u0027t be able to beat the result of getValidatedScoreable called on itself).\n\nThis behaviour is what the system as a whole implements because:\n- This method is only called by unneeded.\n- If this network is the best for any request (not listen), then the \"if (numRequests \u003e 0)\" check in unneeded would return early and the code would not not get here.\n\nWe might want to clarify this in the comments?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 5300,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 5301,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "32a75b0a8d6dfd8b41f248e7cc85e8cdaa490510",
